{"name":"Skylla","hex":"#1f7cc2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Scylla","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Scylla is a legendary, man-eating monster that lives on one side of a narrow channel of water, opposite her counterpart, the sea-swallowing monster Charybdis. The two sides of the strait are within an arrow's range of each other—so close that sailors attempting to avoid the whirlpools of Charybdis would pass dangerously close to Scylla and vice versa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Scylla_Louvre_CA1341.jpg/330px-Scylla_Louvre_CA1341.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scylla","wikidata":"Q193115"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Denarius_Sextus_Pompeius-Scilla.jpg/330px-Denarius_Sextus_Pompeius-Scilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Denarius_Sextus_Pompeius-Scilla.jpg/330px-Denarius_Sextus_Pompeius-Scilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scylla on the reverse of a first-century BC denarius minted by Sextus Pompeius","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADenarius_Sextus_Pompeius-Scilla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Castello_scilla.jpg/500px-Castello_scilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Castello_scilla.jpg/500px-Castello_scilla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Rock of Scilla, Calabria, which is said to be the home of Scylla","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastello_scilla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Scylla_figurine.jpg/500px-Scylla_figuri